      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>matchExpressions</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>array</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>matchExpressions is a list of label selector requirements. The requirements are ANDed.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>matchExpressions[]</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>A label selector requirement is a selector that contains values, a key, and an operator that relates the key and values.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><code>matchLabels</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>object (string)</code></TableCell>
      <TableCell>matchLabels is a map of {"{"}key,value{"}"} pairs. A single {"{"}key,value{"}"} in the matchLabels map is equivalent to an element of matchExpressions, whose key field is "key", the operator is "In", and the values array contains only "value". The requirements are ANDed.</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
      <h3 id="_specnamespaceselectormatchexpressions" class="group scroll-mt-20">.spec.namespaceSelector.matchExpressions<a href="#_specnamespaceselectormatchexpressions" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
